{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1308436-goals-of-2e-scion","id":1308436,"title":"Goals of 2E Scion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-28T01:31:36-07:00","id":1308436,"title":"Goals of 2E Scion","content":"I prepare notes for our Polish FB groups to promote <b>Scion</b> 2E when he will come to sell \u2013 I need to point what where main changes between 1E and 2E of game in it\u2019s rules and setting. As I only heard about 1E, and not know it real - <b>Could you help me with pointing changes in 2E out</b>? Here is my points, add or correct my.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Real world Pantheons</b> \u2013 Gods and myths in 2E strive to be as correct to real world myths as it can be. Game starts in corebook with 10 Pantheons, just to point how diverse are human believes.</li> <li><b>Broadening game experience</b> \u2013 Four variants of Scions ( Born, Created, Chosen, Incranate ), adding Denizens as possible PCs, whole Origin tier of game.</li> <li><b>Using Storypath system </b> \u2013 Made especially for \u2018playing from mortal to god\u2019.</li> </ol>Anything else was a goal of 2E <b>Scion</b>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T05:09:17-07:00","id":1308462,"title":"","content":"In the game flow and rules:<br /> You have much smaller dice pools (it was usual to heroes to roll 15 dice, and gods up to 50).<br /> The numbers to keep control are on a counting scale (no legend pool on the hundreds for gods)<br /> The \u201cmagic\u201d system from 1e is very rigid, while the new system is much more versatile. You need less booms to get more effects, the booms are more like specialisations to make it easier/cheeped to do one effect, while before it was all you could do.<br /> You needed relics for everything except epic attributes, now you may need for attributes, but you can gain access thru guides. You can also get a theme to do magic related indirectly to the purview, as long it\u2019s related to the theme (beaut, animal and passion purview as I recall).<br /> The rules for fate in 2e are more tangible than the 1e (it was annoying for the ST to say when and what would happen to fatebound, and the scions), now there is reason to fatebound, the rules are clear from hero up.<br /> There is more about the rules and game flow, but for now I have this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T09:35:31-07:00","id":1308480,"title":"","content":"I've found that 2e allow you better to differ from your dovine parent/patron than 1e would.<br /> Inheriting 1 calling and 1 purview (at hero) but leaving the rest up to you allows you to feel connected but different from your dovone parent/patron in a way that 1e didnt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T12:51:55-07:00","id":1308509,"title":"","content":"In terms or presentation of &quot;goals&quot; I would change your list up a bit and add one thing:<br /> <br /> 1) The setting is more defined as what he default is (in game called The World). In 1e you weren't told what the expectations where on how the setting differs from the real world since the Pantheons are real and can have a real impact on people. Were all the gods leaving Earth alone thanks to Fate and thus it had been thousands of years since direct influence or visiting Scions, hence the rise of monotheism, and you're playing as things explode again? Was it supposed to be more like the World of Darkness or American Gods were things are there but hidden, waiting to come out when the time is right? Was it supposed to be a slightly different place where Polytheism never completely lost its foothold in the West? 2e decided to answer that (the last one).<br /> <br /> 2) More fidelity* to real world mythology. Two issues with 1e were trying to fit everything into a mold mostly built around the Theoi, and a lack of research. 2e opted to do things to break the mold - such as expanding the ways you can become a Scion - so each Pantheon works more like its mythology says it should world. As well more research was done to, while keeping the Pantheons playable in the system, make them feel more representative of the cultures they came from instead of Western perspectives of them.<br /> <br /> 3) More options for play. The Origin tier was added along with playable denizens (who might be able to become Scions too), and more Pantheons; with more Pantheons promised in future releases. The system was also reworked to be more flexible in how powers work so players don't feel locked into as many specific choices.<br /> <br /> 4) A system designed to handle normal humans in the same scene as Zeus and Vishnu being there. 1e accomplished going from a fresh Scion to a Deity, but wasn't really designed with playing a deity in mind, which gets to be a mechanical mess of giant numbers. 2e was designed specifically to keep things tighter. It uses the Scale system so that instead of Ares and Thor fighting involving massive dice-pools and massive bonuses, they resolve much like two normal humans fighting because they're on the same level the game considers the majority of their power a tie and ignores it for their fight (at least mechanically, the poor surroundings around them is a different matter). The game also focuses on horizontal growth (more variety of powers or more powers you can have on at once) than vertical growth (buying new powers/dots in powers that just make them better).<br /> <br /> * - as a translation issue, I'm not sure how well the difference between &quot;fidelity&quot; and &quot;correct to&quot; comes off. The point is &quot;feel&quot; more than &quot;academic&quot; accuracy even if 2e is better at both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T20:59:00-07:00","id":1308589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1308436-goals-of-2e-scion?p=1308509#post1308509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms or presentation of &quot;goals&quot; I would change your list up a bit and add one thing:<br /> <br /> 1e accomplished going from a fresh Scion to a Deity, but wasn't really designed with playing a deity in mind, which gets to be a mechanical mess of giant numbers. 2e was designed specifically to keep things tighter.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'm hopeful, at present, this is a purely theorhetical comparison. 1e's scale worked fine when constrained to Heroic tier (so much so that the game won awards) and broke down very quickly upon hitting demigod. 2e works fine when constrained to Heroic tier, and we've yet to see any Demigod or God material. Things are looking hopeful, but let's not make unsupported claims or count our chickens before they hatch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1576-mjorkk","name":"mjorkk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T22:01:46-07:00","id":1308597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mjorkk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1308436-goals-of-2e-scion?p=1308589#post1308589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I'm hopeful, at present, this is a purely theorhetical comparison. 1e's scale worked fine when constrained to Heroic tier (so much so that the game won awards) and broke down very quickly upon hitting demigod. 2e works fine when constrained to Heroic tier, and we've yet to see any Demigod or God material. Things are looking hopeful, but let's not make unsupported claims or count our chickens before they hatch.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s the exactly the point of the scale system, you keep playing as usual, but on a higher scale. The problem may surge on as 3+ scale difference combat, as it is impossible for the weaker to damage directly the more powerful, and the more powerful may one hit a bunch of weakers.<br /> <br /> Luckily we have a \u201cdemo\u201d of the inter scale combat as presented for vehicles in Trinity. Of course it\u2019s not a 100% complete combat between demigods, and it\u2019s not detailed, but there are a bunch of suggestions on how to deal with the scale difference ruleswise.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if they don\u2019t do a big change on the way the demigods and gods deal with legend and scale, at least we don\u2019t need to handle 50 dice, and 100+ legend points. What was quite annoying when playing gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}